{
  "_comment": "ZenZork v2 Story 3 (#10565) milestone/trigger defs -- authored data only, the evaluator lives in dojotools_zenzork.yaml mode=milestone. Condition key: 'condition' (checked first) -- 'requires' is accepted as an alias when 'condition' is absent, added as a content-authoring paper-cut fix to match book_lore.json/quest_defs.json's 'requires' naming. Use either name, never both on the same entry (if both are present, 'condition' wins and 'requires' is ignored). Condition vocabulary: achievement, story_complete, notebook_record{type,status}, item, room, landmark, capability, count_gte{type,status,n}, elapsed_since{field,minutes}, all[...], any[...]. achievement/story_complete/story_release (book_lore.json only) are deliberately distinct concepts, per Nathan/Vee: story_release = is this content publicly/playably released (chapter_releases.json's releases[].status); story_complete = has this player completed this story unit (currently only 'prologue', resolved against the engine's computed prologue-complete flag; any other id fails closed/false -- unknown ids are never true); achievement = did this player personally earn this achievement id. Future story_complete ids (e.g. 'episode_01') are a pure engine addition, same one-line pattern, decoupled from legacy achievement names. Effect vocabulary (applied automatically the first time a milestone's condition evaluates true): notebook_write{record_type,text,status,source}, unlock_item{item}, unlock_navpoint{navpoint}, dungeonmind_belief{belief_id,confidence,evidence_seen}, narration_unlock{fragment}, comms_stage{stage}. Episode content itself is authored under #10573, not here -- this file intentionally ships with an empty milestones list. ZenZork v2 Story 11 (#10574): any milestone may also carry an optional 'agent_guidance' object, surfaced per newly-completed milestone in mode=milestone's evaluate result (never merged into narration). Shape: {stance, observed[], claims[], contradictions[], recommended_focus, prohibited_inference[], notebook_delta, confidence} -- all free-form, the engine passes this through unvalidated. Optional for mundane milestones; by convention (not engine enforcement) required for authored story beats. Only ever surfaces when this milestone actually completes, so 'derived from unlocked content only' holds structurally -- same gate as the milestone's other effects. SPOILER CURTAIN (mandatory): 'description', every effects[].text, and agent_guidance.{recommended_focus,notebook_delta,observed[],claims[],contradictions[],prohibited_inference[]} must be base64 at rest -- decoded once at load, same convention as book_lore.json. Plain text in these fields will decode to garbage. id/condition/requires/effects type+record_type+status+source/belief_id/confidence/evidence_seen/agent_guidance.stance/agent_guidance.confidence stay plain (control fields, short tags, not prose).",
